Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and why we need them  
• `year` : groups the observations by calendar year  
• `month` : groups the observations by calendar month  
• `air_temperature` : one of the four temperatures we compare  
• `wetbulb_temperature` : second temperature variable  
• `dewpoint_temperature` : third temperature variable  
• `sea_surface_temp` : fourth temperature variable  

Typical conditions that will be applied  
• `year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2014` – restricts the study period  
• Every temperature column `IS NOT NULL` – avoids biased averages  
• We will aggregate by `(year, month)` and later sort by the computed
  sum‑of‑absolute‑differences

Below are ten progressively more complex BigQuery SQL snippets, each capped
with a brief description.  Replace nothing—table paths and field names are
already correct.  All queries use back‑ticks around identifiers and finish with
`LIMIT 20` (except the final answer).

```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at raw 2010 data and see the four temperature columns.
SELECT
  year, month, day,
  air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
  dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Distinct list of available years in the five tables.
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM (
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2012`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2013`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2014`
)
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Count how many complete (all‑four‑temps present) rows exist in 2013.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS complete_rows_2013
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2013`
WHERE air_temperature       IS NOT NULL
  AND wetbulb_temperature   IS NOT NULL
  AND dewpoint_temperature  IS NOT NULL
  AND sea_surface_temp      IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Average air temperature by month for 2012 (quick sense‑check).
SELECT year, month, AVG(air_temperature) AS avg_air_temp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2012`
WHERE air_temperature IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY year, month
ORDER BY year, month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Bring the five years together (UNION ALL) and sample 20 rows.
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2012`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2013`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2014`
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Compute per‑month averages of the four temperatures for 2011.
WITH yr AS (
  SELECT year, month,
         AVG(air_temperature)      AS avg_air,
         AVG(wetbulb_temperature)  AS avg_wetbulb,
         AVG(dewpoint_temperature) AS avg_dewpt,
         AVG(sea_surface_temp)     AS avg_sst
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011`
  WHERE air_temperature       IS NOT NULL
    AND wetbulb_temperature   IS NOT NULL
    AND dewpoint_temperature  IS NOT NULL
    AND sea_surface_temp      IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY year, month
)
SELECT * FROM yr
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: For each 2013 month, find the pairwise absolute‑difference sum.
WITH mth AS (
  SELECT year, month,
         AVG(air_temperature)      AS a,
         AVG(wetbulb_temperature)  AS w,
         AVG(dewpoint_temperature) AS d,
         AVG(sea_surface_temp)     AS s
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2013`
  WHERE air_temperature       IS NOT NULL
    AND wetbulb_temperature   IS NOT NULL
    AND dewpoint_temperature  IS NOT NULL
    AND sea_surface_temp      IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY year, month
)
SELECT
  year, month,
  ABS(a - w) + ABS(a - d) + ABS(a - s) +
  ABS(w - d) + ABS(w - s) + ABS(d - s) AS sum_abs_diff
FROM mth
ORDER BY sum_abs_diff
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Same as (7) but union 2010‑2012 (multi‑year example).
WITH base AS (
  SELECT year, month,
         air_temperature      AS a,
         wetbulb_temperature  AS w,
         dewpoint_temperature AS d,
         sea_surface_temp     AS s
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, air_temperature, wetbulb_temperature,
         dewpoint_temperature, sea_surface_temp
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2012`
)
, clean AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM base
  WHERE a IS NOT NULL AND w IS NOT NULL AND d IS NOT NULL AND s IS NOT NULL
)
, agg AS (
  SELECT year, month,
         AVG(a) AS a, AVG(w) AS w, AVG(d) AS d, AVG(s) AS s
  FROM clean
  GROUP BY year, month
)
SELECT year, month,
       ABS(a-w)+ABS(a-d)+ABS(a-s)+ABS(w-d)+ABS(w-s)+ABS(d-s) AS sum_abs_diff
FROM agg
ORDER BY sum_abs_diff
LIMIT 20;
```

